APPROVE

REASONS:
- `validate_product_evidence` enforces the intended schema checks: top-level must be a dict; known slices must be dicts; each declared field is type-checked when present; `bool` is explicitly rejected for `int` fields via the guard, matching the capture-bug prevention requirement. `unknown top-level keys are ignored` by design. See `[harness/build_soak/product_evidence.py](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/product_evidence.py:1)`.
- `write_product_evidence(..., strict=True)` calls validation first and raises before any write, so malformed input cannot be emitted under default usage. The strict failure/no-write behavior is explicitly covered by tests. See `[harness/build_soak/product_evidence.py](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/product_evidence.py:63)` and `[harness/build_soak/tests/test_product_evidence_writer.py](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/tests/test_product_evidence_writer.py:67)`.
- `write_provider_ledger` writes one JSON object per line as required, and line format is stable/read-consumable by the tolerant ledger reader used by the oracle path. See `[harness/build_soak/product_evidence.py](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/product_evidence.py:75)` and `[harness/build_soak/tests/test_product_evidence_writer.py](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/tests/test_product_evidence_writer.py:101)`.
- The loop tests correctly validate end-to-end semantics through `classify_run_folder` and oracle verdicts for PASS, PREVIEW ownership failure, and provider failure paths, which aligns with contract intent. See `[harness/build_soak/tests/test_product_evidence_writer.py](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/tests/test_product_evidence_writer.py:82)` and `[.../tests/test_product_evidence_writer.py](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/tests/test_product_evidence_writer.py:101)`.

